               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate calendar="#gregorian" notBefore="1400" notAfter="1419">s. xv
                        in</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <!-- Check if person_3988 is live-->
                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_910">Shere, Surrey. Chantry
                        chapel</orgName><p>The missal was donated in 1477 by <persName
                           key="person_3988" role="dnr">Johannes Cantmell</persName>, 'capellanus
                        cantarie de S.' See the list of donors in the second edition of Medieval
                        Libraries of Great Britain (1964), p. 324.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Helmington Hall, <persName role="fmo">Lord
                        Tollemache</persName>, 72. This was the current location as reported in the
                     second edition (1964).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Acquired, split up and sold by Duschnes, New
                     York' according to the supplement to Medieval Libraries of Great Britain
                     (1987), p. 74. The book appeared in the index of untraced manuscripts and
                     printed books with a footnote: 'some fragments traced' (p. 140). No further
                     details were given.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">A fragment was sold by Charles Edwin Puckett
                     (Inventory# IM-13620, <ref
                        target="https://www.cepuckett.com/inventory/index.php?no_cache=20260731052548&amp;main_page=product_info&amp;products_id=4007"
                        >online description</ref> accessed 31 July 2026). The vendor refers to
                     another leaf in a different bookseller's catalogue, also now untraced: " A
                     sister leaf with a nearly identical large illuminated initial is pictured &amp;
                     described in Rendell, <title>The Medieval World</title>, 1979, item 81."
                     Compare Schoenberg Database of Manuscripts <ref
                        target="https://sdbm.library.upenn.edu/entries/3532"
                     >SDBM_3532</ref>.</provenance>
               </history>
